# aurora.local / packages/storage/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/storage/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here. Copy or merge into packages/storage/pins.env to adopt.
#
# See dev/notes/pinnable-versions-progress.md for the full inventory and
# reasoning behind every choice in this file.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run.
# compose.yml is untouched by this work.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# dockurr/samba (registry path has two r's; the GitHub repo is
# dockur/samba) replaces dperson/samba, which had no release and no
# version tag at all in five years — see the entry this replaces, kept
# in git history for the record. dockurr/samba tracks Samba's own
# release train: 4.23.10 pushed 10 days before this check, with 4.23.8
# and 4.23.7 before it roughly a month apart. Installs exactly two
# packages (samba, libauth-samba) — no Avahi, no wsdd, no nmbd, which
# matters here because the host runs its own avahi-daemon and a
# container-side mDNS responder would have fought it for UDP 5353.
# `:latest` and `:4.23.10` resolve to the identical manifest-list digest
# below, so this is not a downgrade from a fresh pull today. Multi-arch
# (confirmed via `docker buildx imagetools inspect`): linux/amd64,
# linux/arm64, linux/arm/v7 — covers both the Optiplex (amd64) and a Pi
# (arm64). Base is alpine:edge (a rolling branch), accepted because
# pinning by digest makes the image reproducible regardless of that.
# Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_SAMBA=dockurr/samba:4.23.10@sha256:6164872d767ead51d4a6ee9f6449b0a3577f875cefcc85525f9e184dbd5da16d

# vladgh/minidlna — actively maintained (Docker Hub shows a push roughly
# a month before this check, i.e. mid-2026, comfortably past the
# two-week bar). Latest semver-tagged release is 1.3.10. Multi-arch:
# linux/amd64, linux/386, linux/arm/v6, linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64 —
# confirmed via `docker buildx imagetools inspect`; covers both the
# Optiplex (amd64) and a Pi (arm64). No exact release date was available
# in the image's own annotations; the "about a month ago" figure comes
# from the Docker Hub tags listing itself, not a project changelog —
# worth a spot-check before relying on it for the fortnight rule. Checked
# 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_MINIDLNA=vladgh/minidlna:1.3.10@sha256:195a6b6aad3d3940275c4661d6aeeb38ddc71bbe94ed67861f2ab57a4ef69dac
